WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.570
They're epically cool.

2
00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:04.310
And living the lives that we all strive to live.

3
00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:08.520
For decades, The San San Dieguito's Boogie Board Club

4
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.430
has met every week to catch some waves together

5
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.890
and today they're here to tell us about it.

6
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:18.970
So please welcome Fran Dyer, Christa Stahl,

7
00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:22.014
Carol German, and Charlotte Gumbrell.

8
00:00:22.014 --> 00:00:25.635
(audience applauding)

9
00:00:25.635 --> 00:00:26.909
Well hello.

10
00:00:26.909 --> 00:00:29.742
We're so excited to speak with you guys today,

11
00:00:29.742 --> 00:00:32.870
Fran and Christa, you're the founders

12
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.190
of this whole operation.

13
00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:37.152
May I ask, how did it start?

14
00:00:37.152 --> 00:00:40.160
Well, it started in 2002.

15
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.510 line:15%
Christa and I were at a Weight Watchers meeting

16
00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.400 line:15%
and the Weight Watcher meeting was right on the ocean.

17
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.300 line:15%
We were at the top of a bluff

18
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.880 line:15%
and we had 150 steps to walk down to the ocean.

19
00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.437 line:15%
And so I said, "Christa, after the meeting's over,

20
00:00:54.437 --> 00:00:56.607
"why don't we start going in the ocean?

21
00:00:56.607 --> 00:00:58.097
"Why don't we grab some boogie boards

22
00:00:58.097 --> 00:01:00.260 line:15%
"and just go and play?"

23
00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:03.350 line:15%
And three other women joined us and we began.

24
00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.390
And that is 19 years ago.

25
00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:09.033
And Christa, tell us all about your experience with it.

26
00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.397 line:15%
Well, it's pretty much the same.

27
00:01:12.397 --> 00:01:17.010 line:15%
The club that we belong to is a newcomer's club.

28
00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.500 line:15%
And I was new to the area.

29
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:24.190
I retired and I had relocated.

30
00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:27.030
And so it really was a nice meeting up

31
00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.580
and it's been consistent ever since then.

32
00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.700
Fran, I think you've kept me going.

33
00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.693
And perhaps me too.

34
00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:39.789
Carol, you joined the club 15 years ago

35
00:01:39.789 --> 00:01:43.890
after a boogie boarding injury, but it didn't stop you.

36
00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:45.783
Can you tell us about that?

37
00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.540
Well, I also was new to the area

38
00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.690
and really didn't know very many people

39
00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.570 line:15%
and I live right on the ocean.

40
00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:00.930 line:15%
I can look out my window and see it anytime I want

41
00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:04.370
but I wasn't going in because I had broken a number

42
00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.560
of bones boogie boarding in Hawaii.

43
00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:07.420
Oh wow.

44
00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.500
These ladies, when I got to know them

45
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.530
through the main, the big club,

46
00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:14.500
the newcomers club, said, "Come on in the ocean with us."

47
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.800
And Christa was really one of my heroes

48
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.130
because she's a little older than I am.

49
00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:24.320
And I thought, if Christa can do this, I can do it too.

50
00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.540
So they kind of talked me back into the water.

51
00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.920
And I'm so glad they did

52
00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.600
because it keeps us young and healthy.

53
00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.748
I love this so much because I feel like

54
00:02:34.748 --> 00:02:38.380
so many times people just get boring as they get older

55
00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:39.860
and they don't try new things.

56
00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:43.180
And I know Charlotte, you're one of the most senior

57
00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.700
of the boogie boarders, right?

58
00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.830
Tell us how you got into this.

59
00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:51.170 line:15%
Well, actually I wish I'd known about this group earlier.

60
00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:55.530 line:15%
I boogie boarded pretty much with my teenage children.

61
00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:59.180
We use to use the canvas things.

62
00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:02.150
And then all of a sudden somebody invented the boogie board

63
00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:05.209
and oh my golly, what a wonderful thing that was.

64
00:03:05.209 --> 00:03:07.460
So I bought it for grandchildren.

65
00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:09.130
And then I decided that,

66
00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.810
hey I'm the one who really loves to boogie board.

67
00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:14.210
So I've been doing it ever since.

68
00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.623
I think I'm on my fourth board.

69
00:03:16.623 --> 00:03:17.842
What's the best thing about it?

70
00:03:17.842 --> 00:03:21.630
I just have to ask, what really rocks it for you, Charlotte?

71
00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:24.370
Well, in a very short time,

72
00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.960
I feel like my brain is alive.

73
00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:30.750
I'm alive and life is worth living.

74
00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.400
You know, it doesn't take much time

75
00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.560
in that water to feel that way.

76
00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.780
Boogie boarding is a wonderful sport,

77
00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.248
up until, I keep thinking this is my last year

78
00:03:41.248 --> 00:03:43.410
but I'm still doing it.

79
00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.700
You know, friends are everything.

80
00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.730
And the way that you guys show up for each other

81
00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:53.000
and for life in general, is just inspiration to us all.

82
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.700
And thank you for coming to talk here today

83
00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.850
with us so that we can look to you guys

84
00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:00.354
on how we're supposed to live our lives.

85
00:04:00.354 --> 00:04:01.945
(audience applauding)

86
00:04:01.945 --> 00:04:03.863
Thank you for having us.

87
00:04:03.863 --> 00:04:06.786
Thank you so much, we love it.

88
00:04:06.786 --> 00:04:11.750
Thank you Fran, and Christa and Carol and Charlotte.

89
00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:12.583
Thank you

90
00:04:12.583 --> 00:04:14.866
for showing us the way.
Thank you so much.

91
00:04:14.866 --> 00:04:18.220
And cowabunga, we're coming to get ya.

92
00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:19.615
I'll see ya on the waves ladies.

93
00:04:19.615 --> 00:04:21.174
(laughing)

94
00:04:21.174 --> 00:04:24.283
Bye bye.
Thank you so much.

95
00:04:24.283 --> 00:04:26.866 line:15%
(upbeat music)

